    gist: 'A Met Eireann surface analysis chart (synoptic chart) maps the state of the atmosphere at one moment. The closed loops are isobars - lines joining places of equal air pressure - and tightly packed isobars mean a steep pressure gradient and strong winds. Each low pressure centre is marked with an L and its central pressure (the lowest value), each high with an H. Storm Ashley is a deep depression with bands of cloud and rain along its fronts: a warm front (rounded bumps), a cold front (triangular spikes), and where the faster cold front catches the warm front, an occluded front (alternating bumps and spikes) that wraps around the low\'s centre. To answer chart questions: find each L and H, read the central-pressure value printed beside the symbol, name lines of equal pressure as isobars, and identify a front by the shape of its symbols.',
