      label: 'Match the process to where it sits in the cycle',
      text: 'These matching questions are won by reading the position of each number on the diagram, not guessing. The number at the surface, where exposed rock is broken down before transport and deposition, is weathering and erosion. The number beside the sediment/sedimentary rock, where loose deposits are pressed into solid rock, is compaction and cementation. The number on the rising magma path, where molten rock cools and solidifies, is crystallisation of magma. Trace each number to the rock it produces and name the process accordingly.',
