      modelAnswer: '(i) Go up from x = 2.5 to the curve, then across to the y-axis: k(2.5) ≈ 5.8 (the marking scheme accepts any y from 5.5 to 6). (ii) Draw the line y = 7; it meets the curve at about x ≈ 1.9 (the scheme accepts roughly 1.7 ≤ x < 2). The curve is decreasing, so it stays on or below 7 to the RIGHT of that point: k(x) ≤ 7 for x ≥ 1.9 — i.e. 1.9 ≤ x ≤ 5 within the given domain. Show the vertical guide-line for part (i) and the horizontal line y = 7 for part (ii) on the graph to earn the work marks.',
      needed: ['Reading a y-value off a curve: vertical line up from the x-value to the curve, then horizontal across to the y-axis (k(2.5) ≈ 5.8, accept 5.5–6)', 'Solving an inequality from a graph: draw the line y = 7, find where it meets the curve (x ≈ 1.9, accept 1.7 ≤ x < 2), read the x-values that keep the curve on/below it', 'The function is decreasing, so k(x) ≤ 7 to the RIGHT of the crossing point: x ≥ 1.9 (i.e. 1.9 ≤ x ≤ 5 within 0 ≤ x ≤ 5)', 'Showing the guide-lines on the graph — Scale 15D awards marks for the working shown, not only the final estimate'],
