      text: 'The 2021 OL scheme awards each family structure 2 points @ 3 marks (graded 3:2:0), so a bare definition (\'a nuclear family is parents and children\') caps you at one point. Bank a second descriptive detail for each: nuclear → self-contained, shared tasks, relatives dispersed/isolated in crisis; one-parent → arises through separation/divorce/death, more reliant on State benefits, financial/childcare strain; blended → arises through remarriage, large extended family, step-parent discipline issues. Naming a structure without describing it, or describing only one of the three asked, leaves marks on the table.',
