    gist: 'An Tuiseal Ginideach = the \'of the\' form, used when one noun owns or describes another: \'doras an tí\' (the door OF THE house), \'lár na cathrach\' (the centre OF THE city), \'i rith na bliana\' (during the year). The noun usually CHANGES its ending and often takes séimhiú or a slender vowel: \'an chathair\' → \'na cathrach\'; \'an scoil\' → \'i lár na scoile\'. Examiners reward Saibhreas (richness): the OL marking scheme prizes \'nathanna cainte agus frásaí oiriúnacha\' (good phrases and idioms) under Cumas Gaeilge. So learning a handful of ready-made ginideach phrases gives you BOTH correct grammar AND richness marks at once: \'ag deireadh an lae\', \'le himeacht aimsire\', \'i rith na bliana\'.',
    oneMove: {
      label: 'Bank 5 ready-made ginideach phrases — they win Cruinneas AND Saibhreas together',
      text: 'Instead of risking the declension live, memorise correct whole phrases and drop them in: \'i rith na seachtaine\' (during the week), \'ag deireadh an scéil\' (at the end of the story), \'muintir na háite\' (the local people), \'fadhbanna an tsaoil\' (life\'s problems), \'i lár na cathrach\' (in the city centre). Each one is a correct genitive AND a \'nath cainte\' the scheme rewards under Saibhreas. The classic slip is leaving the noun in its plain form (\'lár an cathair\' instead of \'lár na cathrach\').',
    },
    check: {
      prompt: 'Ceartaigh an tuiseal ginideach sna frásaí seo agus mínigh: (i) \'ag deireadh an *lá*\', (ii) \'muintir an *áit*\'. (Correct the genitive in each phrase.)',
      modelAnswer: '(i) \'ag deireadh an lae\' — athraíonn \'lá\' go \'lae\' sa ghinideach (the noun \'lá\' changes to \'lae\' = at the end of the day). (ii) \'muintir na háite\' — \'an áit\' (baininscneach) → \'na háite\' sa ghinideach, le \'h\' roimh an nguta (the people of the place/area). Both are correct genitives and useful \'nathanna\' that earn Saibhreas marks.',
      needed: ['\'ag deireadh an lae\' — \'lá\' → \'lae\'', '\'muintir na háite\' — \'an áit\' → \'na háite\'', 'Notes these double as richness/\'nathanna\' phrases (Saibhreas)'],
    },
    source: 'LC Irish syllabus — Stór Focal agus Nathanna; SEC Irish OL marking scheme 2025 — Cumas Gaeilge strand \'Fairsinge, saibhreas... nathanna cainte agus frásaí oiriúnacha\' (p.10); HL marking scheme 2025 Ceist 6(a) tests \'ainmfhocal baininscneach sa tuiseal ginideach uatha\' (p.21)',
    marksWeight: 9,
