    focus: 'Cén fáth? — the full reason', level: 'ordinary',
    gist: 'The question word tells you the SHAPE of the answer. Match it and the answer almost writes itself. CÉN FÁTH? = why → give a reason, usually starting \'Chun…\' (in order to) or \'Mar…\' (because). CÉ MHÉAD? = how much/many → a number. CÁ / CÉN ÁIT? = where → a place. CÉN NÓS? = what custom → name the custom. The method: read the question word first, find the matching paragraph (the question often names it, e.g. \'Alt 1\'), then take the phrase that answers that exact shape. Sa Léamhthuiscint OL, glactar go rialta le freagra a thógtar díreach as an sliocht (there is no \'own words\' rule at Ordinary level the way Higher has at 6(b)) — so the safe move is to copy the relevant phrase from the passage.',
