    gist: 'A valid contract is a legally binding agreement, and it must contain certain essential elements. The most commonly examined are: Offer and Acceptance (one party makes a clear offer, the other accepts it unconditionally); Consideration (each party gives something of value — usually money, but it can be anything of value); Capacity to Contract (each party is legally able to enter the contract — e.g. not a minor or intoxicated); Consent to Contract (both agree of their own free will, with no undue influence); Intention to Contract (both intend to be legally bound); and Legality of Form / Legality of Purpose (the contract is for a lawful purpose and, where required, is in writing).',
