    gist: 'PAYE (Pay As You Earn) is how income tax is collected from wages by the employer before you are paid. To work out net (take-home) pay you start from Gross Pay, then subtract three deductions: PAYE income tax (a % of gross, then LESS your tax credit, which reduces the tax you owe), PRSI and USC. A TAX CREDIT is not a deduction itself — it is subtracted FROM the PAYE figure, so it lowers the tax. Add up the three deductions (Net PAYE + PRSI + USC) to get Total Deductions, then Gross Pay − Total Deductions = Net Annual Take-Home Pay.',
    oneMove: {
      label: 'Subtract the tax credit from PAYE, not from gross pay',
      text: 'The single most common mistake is treating the tax credit as another deduction off the total, or forgetting it entirely. The correct order is: Net PAYE = (rate × gross) − tax credit. The 2024 OL scheme allows one mark per correct figure/method, so even if one line is wrong you keep marks for the lines that follow if your method is right — always show every step.',
    },
    check: {
      prompt: 'Gemma\'s gross pay is €38,000. Deductions: PAYE = 20% of gross LESS a tax credit of €3,550; PRSI = 4% of gross; USC = 3% of gross. Calculate (a) the net PAYE she pays, (b) her total deductions, and (c) her net annual take-home pay. Show your workings.',
      modelAnswer: '(a) PAYE = (20% × €38,000) − €3,550 = €7,600 − €3,550 = €4,050. (b) PRSI = 4% × €38,000 = €1,520; USC = 3% × €38,000 = €1,140; Total Deductions = €4,050 + €1,520 + €1,140 = €6,710. (c) Net take-home pay = €38,000 − €6,710 = €31,290.',
      needed: ['PAYE before credit = 20% × €38,000 = €7,600', 'Tax credit subtracted from PAYE → Net PAYE €4,050', 'PRSI €1,520 + USC €1,140 added to Net PAYE to give Total Deductions €6,710', 'Net take-home = Gross €38,000 − €6,710 = €31,290'],
    },
    source: 'LC Business — Unit 4: Managing 2 (Aspects of Taxation). SEC Leaving Certificate Business 2024 Ordinary Level, Section 1 Q8 (net annual take-home pay). Marking scheme 2024: 10m, \'If required, allow one mark per figure/method for workings\' — Net PAYE €4,050, PRSI €1,520, USC €1,140, Total Deductions €6,710, Net Annual Take-home Pay €31,290.',
    marksWeight: 10,
