    id: 'biz-bep-chart-label',
    subjectId: 'business', topicId: 'business-4-8',
    subjectLabel: 'Business', topicLabel: 'Finance, Ownership, Production',
    focus: 'Reading a break-even chart', level: 'ordinary',
    gist: 'A break-even chart plots money (Sales / costs, €) up the side against Output in units along the bottom. Three lines matter: Fixed Costs (FC) is a flat horizontal line because it stays the same at every output (rent, insurance). Total Costs (TC) starts at the FC level and rises as you make more (FC + variable costs). Total Revenue (TR) starts at zero (sell nothing, earn nothing) and rises steeply. The Break-Even Point (BEP) is where TR crosses TC — total revenue exactly covers total costs, so there is no profit and no loss. Left of the BEP the firm makes a loss; right of it, a profit.',
    oneMove: {
      label: 'Identify each line by where it STARTS',
      text: 'TR starts at the origin (0,0) and is the steepest — sell nothing, earn nothing. FC is the flat line that never moves. TC starts up at the FC level (not at zero) because even with zero output you still pay fixed costs, then rises. BEP is the single point where TR and TC cross. Students who mix up TC and FC, or who put TR starting above zero, throw away easy marks.',
    },
    check: {
      prompt: 'On the break-even chart shown, four label boxes (A, B, C, D) point to features of the chart. Match each label to: Total Revenue (TR), Total Costs (TC), Fixed Costs (FC), Break-Even Point (BEP). Give one reason for the FC and the BEP choices.',
      modelAnswer: 'B = Total Revenue (the steepest line, starting from the origin). C = Total Costs (rises less steeply, starting up at the fixed-cost level). D = Fixed Costs (the flat horizontal line — it does not change with output). A = Break-Even Point (where the TR and TC lines cross, so total revenue exactly equals total costs — no profit, no loss). FC reason: it is constant at every output, so it must be the flat line. BEP reason: it is the crossing point of TR and TC where revenue covers all costs.',
      needed: ['FC = flat horizontal line (D) — costs unchanged by output', 'BEP = where TR and TC cross (A) — revenue = total cost, no profit/loss', 'TR is the steepest line from the origin (B); TC rises from the FC level (C)'],
    },
    source: 'LC Business — Unit 5: Business in Action (finance & production). Marking scheme 2025 (Ordinary Level), Section 1 Q4 — break-even chart labelling, 10m: B=Total Revenue 3, A=Break-Even Point 3, C=Total Cost 2, D=Fixed Cost 2',
