    gist: 'New Product Development (NPD) is the process of turning an idea into a product that is ready to sell. Three middle stages are tested most: a Feasibility Study checks whether the idea can actually work — is it technically sound and safe (does it meet government regulations), and is it financially viable (will there be enough demand at a selling price that covers all costs)? Break-even analysis is done here. Prototype Development builds a working sample or \'mock-up\' so the firm can test what materials are needed, check it meets standards, and make improvements before full-scale production. Test Marketing trials the product on a small sample of real customers; their feedback decides whether to launch it fully or change it first.',
