      label: 'Background vs event — and never mix the two auxiliaries',
      text: 'When you tell a story, ask of each verb: is this the SCENE (imparfait) or the THING THAT HAPPENED (passé composé)? \'C\'était le matin, il faisait froid (scene), et puis le bus est arrivé (event).\' The examiner\'s Language grid rewards \'verbs generally correct\' and tenses handled well; the classic mark-loser is using the imparfait for a single completed action (\'hier je mangeais\' instead of \'hier j\'ai mangé\').',
