      label: 'Match the article and adjective to the noun\'s gender — \'mon/ma\' is the easy mark to lose',
      text: 'Before you write a noun, lock its gender, then make a/le/un and any adjective agree. The famous OL slip is the possessive: it agrees with the noun, NOT with you — \'ma chambre\' (chambre is feminine) even if a boy is speaking. The HL scheme literally underlines and penalises \'mon chambre\' as a heard grammar error. On OL the Language band rewards \'agreements correct more often than incorrect\', so a handful of fixed agreements lifts your band.',
