      modelAnswer: '(a) The mixture turns a DARKER brown. Increasing temperature favours the endothermic direction (the reverse reaction, since the forward reaction is exothermic), making more brown NO2. (b) The mixture turns PALER. Increasing pressure favours the side with fewer gas molecules — the forward reaction (2 mol → 1 mol) — making more colourless N2O4.',
