    focus: 'SHM: spring period & max acceleration', level: 'higher',
    gist: 'Hooke\'s law (F = -kx) feeds straight into SHM for a mass on a spring. The exam almost always runs the same chain: find the elastic constant k from the static stretch, then use omega = sqrt(k/m) to get period T = 2 pi / omega, then a_max = omega^2 * A. The marks live in keeping units in SI and reading the amplitude A correctly as the distance pulled from the equilibrium (rest) position, not from the natural length.',
