      text: 'Find k from the STATIC stretch: k = mg / x, using the extension from natural length (here x = 0.185 - 0.150 = 0.035 m, so k = (0.2)(9.8)/0.035 = 56 N/m). Then omega = sqrt(k/m). The amplitude A for a_max is the distance from the EQUILIBRIUM position you pull to (200 mm - 185 mm = 15 mm = 0.015 m), NOT from the 150 mm natural length. a_max = omega^2 * A and the speed there is zero because the object is momentarily at rest at the extreme.',
