      modelAnswer: '(i) At equilibrium the spring force balances weight: kx = mg, with extension x = 0.185 - 0.150 = 0.035 m. k = mg/x = (0.200)(9.8)/0.035 = 1.96/0.035 = 56 N m^-1. (ii) omega = sqrt(k/m) = sqrt(56/0.200) = sqrt(280) = 16.73 rad s^-1. T = 2 pi / omega = 2 pi / 16.73 = 0.375 s. (iii) Amplitude A = distance from equilibrium (185 mm) to release point (200 mm) = 0.015 m. a_max = omega^2 * A = 280 * 0.015 = 4.2 m s^-2. (iv) At maximum acceleration the mass is at the extreme of its motion (amplitude), so its speed is zero.',
