    gist: 'The laws of equilibrium experiment asks you to verify two things: sum of upward forces = sum of downward forces (first law), and sum of clockwise moments = sum of anticlockwise moments about a chosen point (second law). The mark-losers are forgetting the metre stick\'s OWN weight acting at its 50 cm centre of gravity, and mixing up which forces turn the stick clockwise versus anticlockwise about the pivot point.',
