      modelAnswer: '(i) Upward forces = 6 + 4 = 10 N. Downward forces = the two hanging weights plus the stick\'s own weight = 5 + 2 + 3 = 10 N. Upward = downward = 10 N, so the first law of equilibrium is verified. (ii) Moment = Force x distance from 0 cm. The downward forces (hanging weights + stick weight) produce clockwise moments: (5 x 26) + (3 x 50) + (2 x 60) = 130 + 150 + 120 = 400 N cm. The upward spring forces produce anticlockwise moments: (6 x 20) + (4 x 70) = 120 + 280 = 400 N cm. Clockwise moments = anticlockwise moments = 400 N cm, so the second law of equilibrium is verified.',
