    gist: 'The photoelectric question gives you light (a wavelength or frequency) hitting a metal with a known work function, and asks for the maximum speed of the emitted electrons. The whole thing is one equation: hf = phi + 1/2 m v^2. Students lose marks by mixing units - the work function is given in eV but everything in the equation must be in joules. Convert wavelength to frequency, convert eV to J, subtract to get the kinetic energy, then solve for v.',
