      modelAnswer: '(i) Mass per unit length uses the full string: mu = m/l = (0.21e-3 kg)/(0.65 m) = 3.23e-4 kg m^-1. The fundamental frequency is f = (1/2L)*sqrt(T/mu), where the vibrating length L = 0.341 m (the gap between the two fixing points), not 0.65 m. Rearranging: T = mu*(2*L*f)^2 = 3.23e-4*(2 x 0.341 x 440)^2 = 3.23e-4 x (300.08)^2 = 29.1 N. (ii) f is proportional to sqrt(T). Reducing T by a factor of four reduces f by a factor of sqrt(4) = 2, so the new frequency = 440/2 = 220 Hz.',
