    gist: 'When you plot current I (y-axis) against potential difference V (x-axis) for a metal conductor, the line is straight through the origin and its slope equals I/V = 1/R, NOT R. So the resistance is the INVERSE of the slope: R = 1 / slope. Students lose the answer marks here by quoting R = slope (giving ~0.14 Ω instead of ~7 Ω), or by reading off a single raw data row instead of taking a big triangle on the LINE OF BEST FIT. Watch the arithmetic too: 1 / 0.14 is 7.1, not 7.0. Always state the slope formula, take two well-separated points that sit ON the line, then invert.',
