      modelAnswer: '(a) Ray 1: from the top of the object draw a ray parallel to the principal axis; it reflects off the mirror and passes back through the focal point f. Ray 2: from the top of the object draw a ray through the focal point f; it reflects off the mirror and travels back parallel to the principal axis. The two reflected rays cross beyond the object — that crossing point is the top of the image. The image is real, inverted and magnified. (b) m = v/u = 40/20 = 2. (c) image height = object height × m = 5 × 2 = 10 cm.',
